+# CI triage: build #1203
+
+Root cause: #61 made `LedgerClient.request` start `response.json()` before looking at the status, but the retry branch (429/502/503/504) `continue`s without ever awaiting that promise.
+The new "retries a gateway error page" test returns an HTML 502 page, so the dropped `json()` promise rejects with a SyntaxError that nobody handles; vitest reports it as an unhandled rejection and exits 1 even though every assertion passed.
+The rejection only surfaces after the body stream is read, by which time the next test ("times out slow requests") is running, which is why the log blames it.
+Fix: parse the body only on the paths that use it (success and error mapping), so a retried response's body is never parsed.
